Display help information for acdg.

Usage: acdg help [command]
-h, --help    Print this usage information.

Run "acdg help" to see global options.
Manage authentication (PKCE Loopback OIDC against Zitadel)

Usage: acdg auth <subcommand> [arguments]
-h, --help    Print this usage information.

Available subcommands:
  login     Authenticate via OIDC (PKCE Loopback against Zitadel)
  logout    Revoke refresh token and clear local session
  refresh   Force a refresh of the access/refresh token pair
  status    Show current login status, roles and expiration

Run "acdg help" to see global options.
Patient registry operations (list, get, audit, register, lifecycle).

Usage: acdg patient <subcommand> [arguments]
-h, --help    Print this usage information.

Available subcommands:
  admit       Admit a patient from the waitlist.
  audit       List the audit trail for a patient.
  discharge   Discharge a currently-admitted patient.
  get         Fetch a single patient by id (full detail).
  list        List patients (paginated; supports search, status, cursor).
  readmit     Readmit a previously-discharged patient.
  register    Register a new patient (composite — flags or --from-yaml).
  withdraw    Withdraw a patient from the waitlist.

Run "acdg help" to see global options.
Family member operations (add, remove, assign caregiver, update identity).

Usage: acdg family <subcommand> [arguments]
-h, --help    Print this usage information.

Available subcommands:
  add                Add a family member to a patient (saga: registers in People Context + Registry).
  assign-caregiver   Mark an existing family member as the primary caregiver for a patient.
  remove             Remove a family member from a patient roster.
  update-identity    Update a patient's social identity (type id + optional description).

