.TH ACDG 1 "2026-05-04" "ACDG CLI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acdg \- Operate the ACDG social care system from the command line.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acdg
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ACDG CLI — Operate the social care system from the command line.

Usage: acdg <command> [arguments]

Global options:
-h, --help      Print this usage information.
    --bff       BFF base URL
                (defaults to "http://localhost:3000")
    --output    json | table | yaml (default: auto — tty=table, pipe=json)
                [json, table, yaml, auto (default)]
    --quiet     suppress info logs

Available commands:
  assessment   Update assessment forms (housing, socioeconomic, work-income, education, health, community-support, social-health-summary).
  auth         Manage authentication (PKCE Loopback OIDC against Zitadel)
  care         Care operations (register appointment, update intake info).
  family       Family member operations (add, remove, assign caregiver, update identity).
  health       Service health probes
  lookup       Lookup tables and approval requests (get, batch, create, update, toggle, request).
  patient      Patient registry operations (list, get, audit, register, lifecycle).
  protection   Protection operations (report violation, register referral, replace placement history).
  team         Team management (list, register, get, deactivate, reactivate, reset-password, role).

Run "acdg help <command>" for more information about a command.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS help

.SS auth

.SS patient

.SS family

.SS assessment

.SS care

.SS protection

.SS lookup

.SS team

.SS health

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACDG_BFF_URL
BFF Web base URL (compile-time \fB--dart-define\fR). Default: \fIhttp://localhost:8081\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/acdg/credentials
OIDC session (chmod 600). Created by \fBacdg auth login\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0   Success
.TP
1   Server error (4xx/5xx other than 401)
.TP
2   Authentication required
.TP
3   Network failure
.TP
7   Refresh token invalidated (run \fBacdg auth login\fR)
.TP
64  Usage error (EX_USAGE)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgh\fR(1), \fBgcloud\fR(1) — sibling CLIs with the same PKCE Loopback authentication pattern.
